<headroom-library version="1" id="clean-envelope-quack" category="Clean" order="100" instrument="guitar" style="Funk">
  <description>Greasy auto-wah funk: a compressor evens your picking into an optical envelope filter set to sweep up, then a clean blackface twin. The quack voicing is fixed on a vocal peak around 800 Hz; Quack and Vowel shape it. Dig in for more bark, play light for a rounder tone.</description>
  <tags><tag>Clean</tag><tag>Funk</tag><tag>Envelope Filter</tag><tag>Compressed</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://www.guitarworld.com/gear/guitar-pedals/mu-tron-iii" title="Guitar World: how the Mu-Tron III became a pedalboard icon"/>
    <source url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mu-Tron" title="Mu-Tron (Wikipedia)"/>
    <source url="https://www.hochstrasserelectronics.com/news//envelope-filter-listening-party" title="Hochstrasser Electronics: envelope filter listening party"/>
    <source url="https://reverb.com/news/the-gear-of-the-grateful-dead" title="Reverb: the gear of the Grateful Dead"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
</headroom-preset>
